ade people who don't who didn't  know  anything about him to vote for him  because  also there was a huge anti-corruption  vote in the country more than 50 percent  of peruvians  did not want to vote for keiko fujimori  uh her of his opponent his rival in this  presidency  she had lost two times for the same  reasons  with nearly the same margin of votes  uh 42 000 votes in the last election and  44 000 votes in this election  uh so there was a there was a  combination of factors that  made pedro castillo win first because  keiko fujimori is highly unliked in many  uh among many in the country and then  because castillo had this  this uh message of change of a new  constitution  which he probably won't be able to do or  or deliver but that's what people think  that people think that if  the constitution is changed they their  lives will  will change that laws will help them  have a a better prospect of a future  so uh so this is how pedro castillo from  coming from uh from from being  nearly unknown has won the presidency  all right thank you very much for that  mariana sanchez there live for us  in lima
 

